 "brief": "FLOER COHOMOLOGY AND PENCILS OF QUADRICS — There is a classical relationship in algebraic geometry between a hyperelliptic curve and an associated pencil of quadric hypersurfaces.",
 "extended": "**FLOER COHOMOLOGY AND PENCILS OF QUADRICS**\n\n*IVAN SMITH*\n\n70 pp, 38 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** There is a classical relationship in algebraic geometry between a hyperelliptic curve and an associated pencil of quadric hypersurfaces. We investigate symplectic aspects of this relationship, with a view to applications in low-dimensional topology.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Two contexts; 1.2 The theorem; 1.3 Entropy; 1.4 Representation varieties; 1.5 Instanton Floer homology; 1.7 Homological Mirror Symmetry; 1.8 Another birational motivation; 1.9 Outline of proof; 2 The representation variety; 2.1 Topology; 2.2 Monodromy and degenerations; 2.3 Fibred 3-manifolds; 2.4 Faithfulness; 2.5 A fixed point theorem; 3 The Fukaya category; 3.1 Floer and quantum cohomology",
